\n  requirements before hand-off.\n- The evidence package is submitted through the security review board process to the external certification\n  lab and accepted for triage.\n\n### Risks / Notes\n\n- The accredited lab's historical turnaround is six to nine months, and the security review board meets on\n  a fixed cadence; both are externally controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort. They\n  dominate the schedule of the certification outcome but do not gate any engineering deliverable in this\n  decomposition.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): a compliance evidence package (module inventory, build attestations, test results) is\n  assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44130,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a30beb113d325c9e","agent_id":"ace6ea55804c2e637","session_id":"f37d0be2-e15d-4b1a-8282-2b0c8101e79b","uuid":"551091b8-1e03-4454-a26e-ef01de372c8e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:50:17.525Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
