rough the Platform Operator build pipeline.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- A crypto module inventory for every Platform Operator image in scope exists, classifying each linked\n53\t  cryptographic library as validated or non-validated.\n54\t- No non-validated cryptographic library remains linked in the request path of any remediated Platform\n55\t  Operator image.\n56\t- Functional tests pass with the remediated images running on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster.\n57\t- The build pipeline is green for the remediated images (first execution of the remediated code through\n58\t  the Platform Operator Konflux pipeline succeeds).\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-1 (P0): all serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto\n63\t  modules — Platform Operator portion.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-988037398ae6e219","agent_id":"a7e929e672b4dfe9b","session_id":"f37d0be2-e15d-4b1a-8282-2b0c8101e79b","uuid":"ad9cf8c5-f651-487b-9541-125abe89fc19","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:52:24.500Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-937cd541d33d1002","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
