{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a9dd843fd19e6e9","type":"tool_result","content":"## Base Images & Dependencies\n\n- **No mention of FIPS, openssl, or cryptography libraries anywhere in this content.**\n- Base images are passed as build args, not pinned here: most Python images use `--build-arg BASE_IMAGE=${BASE_IMG}`, while PMML differs with `--build-arg BASE_IMAGE=${PMML_BASE_IMG}`.\n- Base image and tag *values* are defined elsewhere (as make variables) — this file only consumes them.\n\n## Image Naming / Tagging\n\n- Images follow the pattern `${KO_DOCKER_REPO}/${IMG_VAR}:${TAG}` — the registry and version tag come from variables, so no literal tags or digests appear in this file.\n- MCV images append platform suffixes to the tag, e.g. `${MCV_IMG}:${TAG}-minimal`, `-rocm`, `-gaudi`, `-cuda`, `-unified`.\n\n## Build / Push Mechanics\n\n- Builds use buildx: `${ENGINE} buildx build ${ARCH} ...` — `ENGINE` selects the container engine (\"engine set by ENGINE, default docker\").\n- `--load` is used for several builds (controller, llmisvc, localmodel variants, storageInitializer) so images land in the local daemon; others omit it.\n- `GOTAGS` is passed to Go-based images via `--build-arg GOTAGS=${GOTAGS}`.\n- Push targets fall into two styles:\n  1. **Direct push** — a build dependency followed by `push`, e.g. `docker-push-sklearn: docker-build-sklearn` then a `push` command.\n  2. **Rebuild with `--push`** — several targets (localmodel agent, kernelcache agent, predictive) depend on the build target but then run buildx again with `--push` instead of a plain push.\n- Python-server images build from a `python` subdirectory (`cd python && ...`); Dockerfiles are named per component (e.g., `sklearn.Dockerfile`, `huggingface_server.Dockerfile`).\n- One target aggregates the MCV variants: `docker-build-mcv: docker-build-mcv-minimal docker-build-mcv-rocm ...`\n\n**Note:** This Makefile contains no dependency pinning or checksums — to assess base image versions, FIPS compliance, or crypto library usage, you'd need to inspect the referenced Dockerfiles and the definitions of `BASE_IMG`, `PMML_BASE_IMG`, and `TAG`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80bad19ec0ec143d","agent_id":"a181dc655b6c27c7e","session_id":"f37d0be2-e15d-4b1a-8282-2b0c8101e79b","uuid":"c38eb87c-d25e-4908-a6a2-e3b8ee2d92c5","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:58:51.307Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a9dd843fd19e6e9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
