{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac04eb9139150430","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E007\n3\ttitle: FIPS compliance evidence package and certification submission\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E004\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E005\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: -1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 0\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: -1\n19\t  human_process_gates: -1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: Medium\n25\tai_implementability_score: 1\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# FIPS compliance evidence package and certification submission\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tAssemble the FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package for the model serving stack — module inventory, build\n36\tattestations, and test results — and submit it through the security review board process to the external\n37\taccredited certification lab. The engineering completion point is a complete, internally validated\n38\tevidence package that is submitted and accepted for triage; the lab's certification decision and the\n39\treview board's cadence are externally controlled and are tracked as schedule risks, not deliverables.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Consolidate the module inventory from the serving-stack crypto audits (KServe, serving data plane, and\n44\t  Platform Operator images) into a single compliance inventory of cryptographic modules.\n45\t- Collect the build attestations (provenance, SBOM) produced by the serving-stack build pipelines for the\n46\t  remediated images, including the Platform Operator pipeline attestations.\n47\t- Collect the FIPS-mode test results demonstrating correct operation of the remediated images on\n48\t  FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters.\n49\t- Assemble the evidence package in the format required by the security review board and the certification\n50\t  lab, and drive it through the security review board milestone sign-offs to submission to the lab.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- The evidence package contains the complete module inventory, the build attestations for every\n55\t  remediated serving-stack image, and the FIPS-mode test results.\n56\t- The evidence package is internally validated for completeness and consistency against the submission\n57\t  requirements before hand-off.\n58\t- The evidence package is submitted through the security review board process to the external certification\n59\t  lab and accepted for triage.\n60\t\n61\t### Risks / Notes\n62\t\n63\t- The accredited lab's historical turnaround is six to nine months, and the security review board meets on\n64\t  a fixed cadence; both are externally controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort. They\n65\t  dominate the schedule of the certification outcome but do not gate any engineering deliverable in this\n66\t  decomposition.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-2 (P0): a compliance evidence package (module inventory, build attestations, test results) is\n71\t  assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b0ffec040526743","agent_id":"a02b9e912b910f608","session_id":"f37d0be2-e15d-4b1a-8282-2b0c8101e79b","uuid":"eedf2ee3-5b09-4149-b9c4-9e1db542f086","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:01:08.058Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac04eb9139150430","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
